    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is `owners.POST.yml`, a 16-step pipeline; the first seven steps run outside the transaction, and everything from `build` onward runs inside `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Step-by-step\n\n1. **`RequireOwnerFields`**\n   - *Side-effect:* normalizes the **address in place** (`AddressNormalizer`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`/`RD\u2192ROAD`/`AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n   - *Validation:* rejects if any of **firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone** is null/blank **after** normalization \u2192 **400** `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (lists offending fields).\n   - *Side-effect:* republishes the (mutated) body as a variable for later steps.\n\n2. **`ValidatePostcode`** \u2014 *Validation only, postcode optional.* If null, passes. If present it must match `^[0-9]{4}$`; and if the city has a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) the value must fall in that inclusive range. Otherwise \u2192 **400** `InvalidPostcodeException`. (Unknown city + 4 digits = accepted.)\n\n3. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`**\n   - *Side-effect:* rewrites telephone **in place** to E.164 (`E164Telephone`: strip non-digits; keep `+`/country code if present, else assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`).\n   - *Validation:* must yield 8\u201315 digits \u2192 else **400** `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n4. **`ValidateTelephoneCountryLength`** \u2014 *Validation only.* National-number length by country code: `+61` must have exactly 9 national digits, `+1` exactly 10. Other country codes keep only the generic 8\u201315 bound. Wrong length \u2192 **400** `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n5. **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 *email optional.*\n   - *Side-effect:* blank/null email \u2192 set to `null`.\n   - *Validation:* present-but-invalid syntax \u2192 **400** `InvalidEmailException`.\n   - *Side-effect:* valid email \u2192 stored **trimmed and lower-cased**.\n\n6. **`RejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 *Validation.* Counts existing owners in the requested city; if **\u2265 50** \u2192 **409** `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n7. **`RejectDailyLimit`** \u2014 *Validation.* Computes the effective registration date (request's `registrationDate`, else `today`) rolled forward to a business day (`BusinessDay`); if **\u2265 100** owners already registered on that day \u2192 **429** `DailyLimitExceededException`.\n\n*\u2014 transaction begins (all steps below are `govern: [ transaction ]`) \u2014*\n\n8. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 *Side-effect.* Maps the DTO to an `Owner` (`OwnerMapper`); sets `registrationDate` to the effective date (request or today) **rolled forward to a business day**.\n\n9. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 *Side-effect.* Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive, trimmed); excludes the not-yet-saved new owner.\n\n10. **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 *Side-effect.* Sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is a per-city sequence = (existing owners in that city) + 1.\n\n11. **`AssignHousehold`** \u2014 *Side-effect,* only when the request opts in with `sharesHousehold`. If an existing owner matches on normalized last name + normalized address, sets a deterministic `householdId` on the new owner **and backfills+saves** that id onto every matching existing member.\n\n12. **`RejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 *Validation.* Rejects if the new owner's identity key `telephone(E.164) | email(lower) | householdId` exactly matches an existing owner's \u2192 **409** `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n\n13. **`AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 *Side-effect.* Sets `householdSize` = existing owners sharing the `householdId` **plus one** (the new owner); 1 when there is no household id.\n\n14. **`SaveOwner`** \u2014 *Side-effect.* Persists the owner (`ownerRepository.save`), assigning its id.\n\n15. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *Side-effect.* Emits an `AUDIT` log line with owner id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`.\n\n16. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *Side-effect / response.* Maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` (`true` when > 80 owners already registered for today's business day), and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. The transaction commits at pipeline end.\n\n### Notes worth flagging\n- **Ordering matters and is deliberate:** field/format checks (400) run *before* the DB checks; capacity (409) and daily-limit (429) run *before* the transaction; the duplicate-identity check (409) runs *after* `AssignHousehold` because `householdId` is part of the identity key.\n- The `householdId` backfill in step 11 mutates and saves **existing** owners, and it happens *before* the duplicate check and save \u2014 so a request that later throws (e.g. duplicate identity) would roll those backfills back with the transaction.\n- Steps 6, 7, 10, 11, 13, 14, 16 each call `ownerRepository.findAll()` (repeated full scans within one request)."
